course: dictionary
lesson: 6887
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so read the words around them to find the right one. «Leaving you off the list was an oversight, sorry.» Here an oversight is a mistake, because someone forgot or did not notice something.
explain: Oversight can also mean being in charge of something and watching over it. «A committee has oversight of the school budget.» The committee is not making a mistake here. It is looking after the money and making sure it is spent well.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "A committee has a mistake of the school budget" does not make sense, so this sentence needs the second meaning.
fact: An oversight is a mistake made because you forgot or did not notice something.
fact: Oversight can also mean the job of watching over and being in charge of something, as in "oversight of the project".
fact: «A simple oversight» means a small, easy mistake.
fact: «By an oversight» means by accident, not on purpose.
fact: Oversight is a noun: one oversight, two oversights.
exercise: «Leaving you off the list was an oversight, sorry.» What does oversight mean here? | A long journey | A type of list | *A mistake, because someone forgot you | A happy surprise
exercise: «A committee has oversight of the school budget.» What does oversight mean here? | Losing the school keys | *Being in charge of watching over the money | A party for the teachers | A small mistake in the sums
exercise: «The sign was put up by an oversight, not on purpose.» Which word means the same as by an oversight? | On purpose | After a long time | With great care | *By accident
test: Ella says, «We need someone with oversight of the sports day.» What does oversight mean here? | A sports prize | Forgetting the date | A bag of equipment | *Being in charge and watching over it
test: Which phrase means being in charge of something? | *have oversight of | a simple oversight | an oversight list | by an oversight
exam: Which sentence uses oversight to mean a mistake? | The committee has oversight of the school budget. | The head teacher has oversight of the playground. | The team captain has oversight of the rules. | *She missed my birthday by an oversight.
